\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Case Study Interview Summary\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 Core Concept & Vision\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Product:
\f1\b0  A wave terrain synthesizer plug-in that translates physical geographic data\'97such as the height data of Mount Everest to generate a cosmic pad sound\'97into raw audio synthesis.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Thesis:
\f1\b0  Proving that wave terrain synthesis offers unexplored sonic territory and that a deeply visual interface creates a stronger, more intuitive connection between visual data and sound generation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Key UX/UI Challenges & Design Solutions\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Balancing Control & Usability:
\f1\b0  Tackling the tension between giving musicians granular control and making the tool producer-friendly. The speed fader was split into 
\f0\b coarse and fine
\f1\b0  controls to make navigation precise.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Managing Sonic Chaos:
\f1\b0  Wave terrain synthesis can quickly become intensely noisy (sampling miles of data from a simple sine wave cycle). This was addressed by structuring a clean hierarchy with dedicated ADSR and FX sections to quickly tame the sound.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Redefining the Mod Matrix:
\f1\b0  Rejecting the traditional, cumbersome grid-based mod matrix page in favor of 
\f0\b direct, tactile manipulation centered around the morph button
\f1\b0 .\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Innovative Interaction Models:
\f1\b0  Introducing a lighting and hover-state paradigm where knobs and parameters subtly illuminate to show active modulation sources (LFOs, envelopes) without cluttering the interface.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Spatial Feedback:
\f1\b0  Utilizing a dual-view system: a compact, sonar-like crosshair LCD screen for precise instrument readouts, paired with a high-definition Terrain View showing the orbit as a ribbon over the height data.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Next Steps & Validation\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 User Testing Shift:
\f1\b0  Moving from organic, informal synth jams to structured user testing and interviews.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Core Hypothesis to Test:
\f1\b0  Validating whether current draggable affordances and modulatable parameters are obvious enough, and refining the hover-and-light feedback system to ensure seamless discoverability across different hardware setups.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs34 \cf3 \cb4 \outl0\strokewidth0 \
\
I am working on a wavetable synthesizer plug in. My inspiration came from studying DSP in university and was a way to combine my love for music and coding. I want the reader to take away that there are still some synthesis methods unexplored and also that the visual aspect of the synthesis method lends itself to a deeper connection between what creates the sound and what is visually shown. I am planning on releasing the synth with the standard preset of the mount everest and a cosmis pad sound created by its height data\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs34 \cf3 \cb4 I added a LCD screen which has a crosshair to immediately indicate that this is the position where are at. It can be dragged by the mouse. The Terrain View is a larger and more high def version of this small screen and shows the orbit as a ribbon going over the height data(the lcd screen doesn't show height data further associating with a sonar radar).\
\
the current version is actually still kind of a MVP but usable. My final version should have a macro section where you can assign your most valuable knobs to those macro knobs to have an easier access to the controls. But for now I have split the controls for the orbit and the controls for adsr and FX. The main sources of change are Speed(of the orbital traveling), Radius/Squeeze (which determines the area that is sampled) and rotation/position(which determines how steady the sound stays). It is an ongoing process but for now the sections in themselves have a good hierarchy\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf3 \cb5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs34 \cf3 \cb4 The most difficult challenges are the sliders and their range. As a musician you want control but as a producer you want a tool that is easy to use. I split the Speed Fader into coarse and fine. To figure out what is needed for the product to actually feel like an instrument is what is most challenging.\cb1 \
\
\cb4 Also adding the FX section was interesting. I needed to tame the sound more easily because anyone trying out the radius knob will soon find out how noisy the sounds can get when you create them with wave terrain synthesis. You basically take a small waveform like a sine wave and explore maybe kilometres/miles around it in the same amount of time a sinewave cycle needs to complete. This is obviously an exciting range of freedom but to be able to tame these sounds quickly is what is most important there.\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs34 \cf3 \cb4 I am testing with small synth jams and will soon conduct more in-depth user testings and interviews.
\f3\fs24 \cb5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs34 \cf3 \cb4 For me the most challenging part about the synthesizer is the mod matrix. There are different sets of expectations regarding mod matrices in audio plug ins but I had many bad experiences with them myself. In the end it should look elegant but much more it should be easy to use. The handler should look like its draggable. It should be clear what can be modulated. All those things are what really catch me because the power of the synth lies in its vast unending sound creation possibility which is completely lost when we don't make the mod matrix a dream to work with. If this can lead to a good macro page in which one knob turns 30 other knobs and the sound changes completely with one knob than we made it. That is the goal. To take any sound and create somethign exciting with it using this synthesizer.\cb1 \
\
\cb4 My hypothesis is that the handler does not look draggable enough and the knobs and and sliders that are modulatable are not clear enough. I need to test and find solutions for that that are different than having a singular mod matrix page, which would be an easy out but I think modulating the morph button should be the main feature and i will try to make this the easiest function of the synth\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs34 \cf3 \cb4 I would like to take hover as the main source of interaction for this. This goes beyond classical UXUI design I think but staging with light will be part of this in the future. Each knob lights up a little with the mod LFO/env/ADR that it hovers over. And if you hover over the Mod Matrix you see all the connections.\'a0
\f3\fs24 \cb5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Case Study Interview Summary: WT-186 Wave Terrain Synthesizer\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 1. Project Vision & Conceptual Foundation\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Instrument:
\f1\b0  A custom-built wave terrain synthesizer plug-in developed out of a university background in Digital Signal Processing (DSP), combining a passion for code, music production, and unexplored synthesis methods.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Narrative Hook:
\f1\b0  Grounding an abstract mathematical DSP concept in tangible reality by utilizing physical geographic datasets\'97specifically using Mount Everest's height data to generate an organic, sweeping cosmic pad sound.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Core Philosophy:
\f1\b0  Proving that visual interfaces can establish a deeper, more intuitive connection between what creates a sound and how it is visually represented, moving away from sterile menu-diving.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 2. Interface Architecture & Visual Navigation\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Dual-View Feedback Loop:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1
\f4\i \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Sonar LCD:
\f1\i0  A compact, precise screen featuring a crosshair to indicate the exact current position, intentionally echoing a sonar radar aesthetic without displaying overwhelming height data.\
\ls5\ilvl1
\f4\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Terrain View:
\f1\i0  A larger, high-definition visualization showing the orbital path as a flowing ribbon directly traversing the geographic height data.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Layout & Control Hierarchy:
\f1\b0  Carefully structured sections separating orbit mechanics from sound-shaping parameters (ADSR and FX) to maintain a clean, musician-friendly workflow.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 3. Core UX/UI Challenges & Solutions\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Granular Control vs. Playability:
\f1\b0  Balancing the precise demands of musicians with the fast workflow needed by modern producers.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1
\f4\i \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Solution:
\f1\i0  Splitting the orbital Speed fader into 
\f0\b coarse and fine
\f1\b0  controls to tame hyper-sensitive parameter ranges.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Taming Sonic Chaos:
\f1\b0  Wave terrain synthesis inherently risks extreme audio noise when a small waveform (like a sine wave) samples vast stretches of terrain data in a single cycle.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1
\f4\i \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Solution:
\f1\i0  Integrating dedicated, easily accessible FX and macro sections to serve as creative safety rails, allowing producers to dial back chaos quickly and shape usable sounds.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reinventing the Modulation Matrix:
\f1\b0  Moving away from traditional, cumbersome, and often frustrating grid-based mod matrix pages.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1
\f4\i \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Solution:
\f1\i0  Focusing the core interaction around direct manipulation of the morph button, backed by an innovative 
\f0\b contextual lighting and hover-state model
\f1\b0  where parameters subtly illuminate to reveal active modulations (LFOs, envelopes) without cluttering the screen.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 4. User Testing & Validation Strategy\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 From Informal to Formal:
\f1\b0  Transitioning initial product validation\'97which relied heavily on organic, personal synth jams and dogfooding\'97into structured, in-depth user interviews and usability tests.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Key Hypotheses Under Scrutiny:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl1\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Evaluating whether drag affordances on handlers are immediately clear to new users.\
\ls7\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ensuring modulatable knobs and sliders communicate their state effectively without relying on a separate, hidden settings page.\
\ls7\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Exploring the accessibility and discoverability of hover-based lighting paradigms across varied hardware setups.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

